// "Look at the top card of your library. If it's a <TYPE> card, you may reveal
// it and put it into your hand." — the type-gated single-card peek-to-hand
// shape (Frost Augur "snow", Dryad Greenseeker "land", Domri Rade "creature").
//
// No dedicated "look at" atom — composed from primitives like `Explore.ron`
// and `ExileTop.ron`: bind the single top card (`Each` over `TopOfLibrary` 1 ->
// the per-iteration anaphor `It`); looking is the private inspection the peek
// itself grants (the card stays on top, unmoved). The `If` reads the peeked
// card's card type ([CR#300.1]); on a match, a single `May` covers BOTH the
// public reveal ([CR#701.20a] — revealing never moves the card, [CR#701.20b])
// AND the library -> hand move, so "you may reveal it and put it into your
// hand" is one optional two-step sequence, not two independent options.
//
// The `${0}` slot is the card-type word between "a" and "card"; its declared
// `CardTypePredicate` param routes the word through the shared library-search
// classifier (`search_card_descriptor`, migrations effect.rs), which emits the
// CR-correct atom — `Type("Land")`/`Type("Creature")` for a card TYPE, a bare
// `Supertype(Snow)` for a SUPERTYPE ([CR#205.4a]) — so "snow" and "land"
// classify differently rather than blindly wrapping in `Type`.
//
// Renders template-first: `${0}` renders back to the bare word via
// `filter_noun` (`Type(_)` -> its type noun, `Supertype(Snow)` -> "snow"), so
// "If it's a snow card" round-trips.
(
    name: "LookAtTopRevealToHand",
    template: "look at the top card of your library. If it's a ${0} card, you may reveal it and put it into your hand",
    kinds: [OneShotEffect],
    params: [CardTypePredicate],
    body: Each(
        binder: Existing(TopOfLibrary(count: 1)),
        effect: If(
            condition: Matches(It, Param(0)),
            then: May(who: You, effect: Sequentially([
                Reveal(what: It),
                Move(It, Hand),
            ])),
        ),
    ),
)
